ine + fill) — appears at nametable $35, col 23 row 25.\n- CHR $125 = bush body solid fill (bottom middle) — nametable $25, cols 24-29 row 25.\n- CHR $138 = bush bottom-right end (right outline + fill) — nametable $38, col 30 row 25.\n- CHR $136 = bush top-left hump half — nametable $36, cols 24,26,28 row 24.\n- CHR $137 = bush top-right hump half — nametable $37, cols 25,27,29 row 24.\n\nHmm, but wait — is $135 really \"bottom-left\"? Given the region bbox y 192-207 and $35 at row25 col23, yes it's in the lower row. But hmm, in the actual SMB1 bush metatile definition, the bush is 2 rows: top row = $36,$37..., bottom row = $35, $25..., $38. Hmm, but actually I recall the SMB1 bush tiles being named like \"bushLeft\", \"bushMiddle\", \"bushRight\" being $35,$37,$39? Not sure.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider. Looking at $135 pixels again:\n\nrow0: 0 0 0 0 0 3 3 3\nrow1: 0 0 0 0 3 1 1 1\nrow2: 0 0 0 3 1 1 1 1\nrow3: 0 0 0 1 1 1 1 1\nrow4: 0 3 3 1 1 1 1 1\nrow5: 3 1 1 1 1 1 1 1\nrow6: 3 1 1 1 1 1 1 1\nrow7: 0 3 1 1 1 1 1 1\n\nSo $135: the top-right has a diagonal outline going down-left, and the left side has a small outline at rows4-6 col0. The fill is index1. The bottom-left corner (row7 col0) is transparent (0), row7 col1=3.\n\nHmm, so $135's top edge: the diagonal from (7,0) down to (4,2)... so the top surface slopes down to the left. And there's an outline along the left at rows 4-6. So this is the bush's LEFT END with the top-left slope descending. But it's in the LOWER row of the bush? That doesn't fit \"bottom\".\n\nHold on — maybe I mis-assigned rows. Let me recheck the nametable: read_nametable(x=22,y=23,width=10,height=3) returned:\nRow 23: all 24\nRow 24: 24 24 36 37 36 37 36 37 24 24\nRow 25: 24 35 25 25 25 25 25 25 38 24\n\nWait, but the nametable was read with the current scroll (0). Row 24 = y 192-199, row 25 = y 200-207. Hmm.\n\nBut hold on, the read_nametable rows might be off because the HUD... no.\n\nHmm, but the bush visually: in the screen