{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the mapping sheet for the first screen of World 1-1.\n\n## Scene: World 1-1, first screen\nReached from the attract demo by Start (→ title), wait, Start again; verified live: `$0770` = 1, HUD reads `WORLD 1-1`, TIME 395, small Mario on the hill. **The emulator is currently paused on that frame.**\n\n## Small Mario — metasprite (`record_mapping` sprite `small_mario`)\n`list_sprites` proof: 8 OAM entries, all sprite palette 4, no vertical flips, none behind background. It is a 2×2 (16×16) *visible* metasprite drawn in a 2×4 (16×32) sprite form whose top two rows are blank `$FC` filler.\n\n| tile | x/y offset from origin (40,193) | flips | part |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `$FC` (252) | (+0,−16) | none | blank filler |\n| `$FC` (252) | (+8,−16) | none | blank filler |\n| `$FC` (252) | (+0,−8) | none | blank filler |\n| `$FC` (252) | (+8,−8) | none | blank filler |\n| `$3A` (58) | (+0,+0) | none | upper-left (hat top + face/hair) |\n| `$37` (55) | (+8,+0) | none | upper-right (hat brim + face) |\n| `$4F` (79) | (+0,+8) | none | lower-left (shirt/overalls/hand/shoe) |\n| `$4F` (79) | (+8,+8) | **h-flip** (attr `$40`) | lower-right (mirror) |\n\nOAM slot 0 (tile `$FF`, palette 7) is the HUD coin icon, not Mario.\n\n## His colors — sprite palette 4 (`record_mapping` palette `4`)\nLive value `[$0F, $16, $27, $18]`:\n- **slot 0** `$0F` black — transparent (sprite index 0 is never drawn)\n- **slot 1** `$16` red — **hat + shirt/overalls** (proved: set slot 1 to `$2C` cyan, stepped a frame → hat and body turned cyan while the face stayed orange; `clear_palette_overrides` restored `$16`, confirmed `$16` at (45,194)/(49,194))\n- **slot 2** `$27` orange — **skin**: face and hands (rendered `$27` sampled at (45,199) and (43,203))\n- **slot 3** `$18` olive — **dark detail**: hair, eyes/mustache, shoes\n\nIn this scene only Mario uses palette 4 (coin icon and Goomba use palette 7).\n\n## The bush (`get_region` object mode at (210,198), palette 0)\nProof: 709 connected background palette-0 pixels using slots 1,2,3, box (184,192)–(241,207), background pattern table **$1000**. Five CHR tiles, all recorded with group `bush`:\n\n| `record_mapping` id | CHR | part (nametable placement) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `0x25` | `$125` | **bush body fill** — solid index-1 lime block (row 25, cols 24–29) |\n| `0x35` | `$135` | **bush bottom-left** — left slope + left outline of the base (col 23, row 25) |\n| `0x38` | `$138` | **bush bottom-right** — right slope, notch + right outline (col 30, row 25) |\n| `0x36` | `$136` | **bush top-left** — left half of a scallop; placed 3× (row 24, cols 24/26/28) |\n| `0x37` | `$137` | **bush top-right** — right half of a scallop; placed 3× (row 24, cols 25/27/29) |\n\nEach `$36`+`$37` pair meets in a peak → the bush's **three humps**, over a base one tile wider at each end.\n\n`promote_mappings` ran once: **7 discoveries promoted** (23 tiles, 7 palettes, 1 sprite, 26 addresses in the mapping file). No ROM bytes were written — all edits were live/frozen palette changes and were reverted."}
